# Claude #2b: THE BATHTUBS. A ring of n tubs (600) of whole cups of water. Every turn, all at once, each tub
# pours a third of its water (rounded down) into EACH neighbour and keeps the rest. Water is never lost.
use stdlib
: n 600 dig ;
: w 1000 + dig ;
: left dup 1 = if drop n else 1 - then ;
: right dup n = if drop 1 else 1 + then ;
: give w 705 dig / ;
: new dup w over give 2 * - over left give + over right give + swap 3000 + bury ;
: turn 1 [ dup new 1 + dup n > if drop 0 then ] drop 1 [ dup 3000 + dig over 1000 + bury 1 + dup n > if drop 0 then ] drop ;
: look 1001 1000 n + echo ;
: CAP 602 dig ;
: run look drop 0 501 bury 1 [ drop turn 501 dig 1 + 501 bury look dup 500 bury 0 = 501 dig CAP > 0 = * ] drop 500 dig ;
: dice 700 dig 1103515245 * 12345 + 2147483648 % dup 700 bury 65536 / 704 dig % ;
: roll 1 [ dice over 1000 + bury 1 + dup n > if drop 0 then ] drop ;
